# Standard library — one tree

File: ooda/std/README.oot
All product libraries live here, next to the compiler.
This map is first principles, systems order, and power law.
It is not a copy of another language's folder names.

## 1. Laws

  1. One tree.
  2. A library is code that other programs import. A prove file is not a library.
  3. Proof is emit-c + gcc + run. A folder on disk is not a cert.
  4. Effects need a cap.
  5. Power law: a few modules carry most programs. Work those first.
  6. Systems order: compiler floor, then these trunk modules, then the long tail.

## 2. Power law and domain map

  Trunk (do these first)
    core/  collections/  math/  text/
    encoding/  io/  fs/  net/  os/

  Support
    sync/  actor/  hash/  crypto/  sec/
    markup/  archive/  time/  diag/  test/  simd/

  Domain parents (tail lives under these; do not add more parents)
    hw/       silicon: arch, gpu, bare_metal, mem
    compile/  this compiler: llvm, wasm, parsers, token_opt
    phys/     physics laws and constructions
    chem/     chemistry
    bio/      biology
    robot/    robots and vehicles
    econ/     markets
    data/     db, cloud, gis
    ai/       models and swarms
    ui/       tui, gui, media
    principles/  four bounds only: constants, units, Landauer, zero-ambient

  File role is not a folder: a law of physics lives in phys/.
  A math law lives in math/. Principles stay in principles/.

  Not libraries
    each std parent is certified in qa/<domain>/{invariants,adversarial,caps,kat}.oo
    named keepers live in qa/formal_proofs, qa/prove, qa/proof_verifiers

## 3. Use

  Import `std/core/option.oo` and `std/core/list.oo` as before.
  Named product proves live in `ooda/fixtures/prove_prod_*.oo`.

## 4. Residual

  Compiler: generic `Result[T,E]`, richer sums, deeper lists.
  Library: hard-crypto, decompress, full markup, destubs.
  Path freeze: Delta_path = 0 after the canary eviction. No new std/ top-level dirs.

